#
# tetrakishexahedron.obj - Tetrakis hexahedron
#
# Geometry:   a cube with corners at ±1, carrying a pyramid on each face
#             whose apex is at ±1.5 along that axis, a quarter of the cube's
#             edge above it. That shape is the tetrakis hexahedron, and it is
#             closed and convex: 14 vertices, 36 edges and 24 faces give
#             V - E + F = 2, every edge is shared by two faces, and no face
#             plane has the solid on both sides of it. Spiky as it looks, it
#             is no star.
# Components: 14 vertices, no UV coordinates and no normals - the faces carry
#             a 1/1/1 index triple that refers to neither, so the loader
#             derives the vertex normals - and 24 triangular faces, four to a
#             pyramid. Opposite pairs within a pyramid are wound opposite
#             ways, which glenzcube's crossed look is built on rather than an
#             inconsistency to repair.
# Used by:    glenzcube.
#
o tetrakishexahedron
v -1.000000 -1.000000 -1.000000
v -1.000000 -1.000000 1.000000
v 1.000000 -1.000000 1.000000
v 1.000000 -1.000000 -1.000000
v -1.000000 1.000000 -1.000000
v -1.000000 1.000000 1.000000
v 1.000000 1.000000 1.000000
v 1.000000 1.000000 -1.000000
v -1.500000 0.000000 0.000000
v 0.000000 0.000000 1.500000
v 1.500000 0.000000 0.000000
v 0.000000 0.000000 -1.500000
v 0.000000 1.500000 0.000000
v 0.000000 -1.500000 0.000000
f 5/1/1 9/1/1 6/1/1
f 2/1/1 9/1/1 1/1/1
f 5/1/1 9/1/1 1/1/1
f 2/1/1 9/1/1 6/1/1
f 7/1/1 10/1/1 6/1/1
f 2/1/1 10/1/1 3/1/1
f 2/1/1 10/1/1 6/1/1
f 7/1/1 10/1/1 3/1/1
f 7/1/1 11/1/1 8/1/1
f 4/1/1 11/1/1 3/1/1
f 7/1/1 11/1/1 3/1/1
f 4/1/1 11/1/1 8/1/1
f 5/1/1 12/1/1 8/1/1
f 4/1/1 12/1/1 1/1/1
f 4/1/1 12/1/1 8/1/1
f 5/1/1 12/1/1 1/1/1
f 5/1/1 13/1/1 8/1/1
f 7/1/1 13/1/1 6/1/1
f 5/1/1 13/1/1 6/1/1
f 7/1/1 13/1/1 8/1/1
f 4/1/1 14/1/1 1/1/1
f 2/1/1 14/1/1 3/1/1
f 4/1/1 14/1/1 3/1/1
f 2/1/1 14/1/1 1/1/1
